## Why This Is Asked

Assess how CKNE scores translate to practical controls in an API gateway, including per-tenant concurrency, circuit-breakers, and retry budgets, plus a simple scheduling loop and test plan.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-to-resource mapping
- Fairness and SLA preservation
- Lightweight telemetry and safe preemption

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo minute loop
function ckneMinuteLoop(state){
  for (const t of state.tenants){
    if (t.ckne < 0.5) { t.concurrency = Math.max(1, t.concurrency-1); }
    else { t.concurrency = Math.min(state.maxConcurrency, t.concurrency+1); }
    t.retryBudget = t.ckne > 0.7 ? t.retryBudget : 1;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate fairness across tenants during bursts?
- How would you extend this to multi-region deployments?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests real-time traffic allocation, statistical validity, and multi-tenant fairness under CZNE constraints in a practical feature rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-weighted exposure and normalization
- Minute-by-minute reallocation under SLA guarantees
- Deterministic seeding for reproducible experiments
- Telemetry, rollback, and drift detection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: compute per-tenant exposure weights
function computeWeights(tenants){
  const eps = 0.01;
  const sum = tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+(t.ckne+eps),0);
  return tenants.map(t=>({tenant:t.id, weight:(t.ckne+eps)/sum}));
}
```

